  - `scripts/data/document-index/phase-c-classify.py`
  - any existing helper used to read/write `index.jsonl`
- Replace the invented `readability` rubric with a rubric based on verified fields already present in the pipeline, or explicitly add a prerequisite issue if a new field is required.
- Narrow the #2247 handoff contract to what exists now: content-hash-targeted bounded writeback, unless #2247 is separately extended first.
- Define the mapping from index `source` values to mounted source-root ownership so “source-root-first” packs are falsifiable.
- Fix the tests so live `index.jsonl` is the primary authority and audit/registry counts are reconciliation checks, not the source of truth.
- Constrain proposed domain/writeback outputs to currently valid authoritative taxonomy values.
